## 📌 `enqueue(int value)` → Insert at **rear**
```c
void enqueue(int value) {
    struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    newNode->data = value;     // store the value
    newNode->next = NULL;      // new node will be last, so next = NULL

    if (rear == NULL) {        // if queue is empty
        front = rear = newNode; // both front & rear point to newNode
    } else {
        rear->next = newNode;   // link newNode after current rear
        rear = newNode;         // update rear to newNode
    }
}
```
👉 **Think:** People join the line from the back.  

---

## 📌 `dequeue()` → Remove from **front**
```c
void dequeue() {
    if (front == NULL) {       // if queue is empty
        printf("Queue is empty\n");
        return;
    }
    struct Node* temp = front; // take the front node
    front = front->next;       // move front to next node
    if (front == NULL) rear = NULL; // if queue became empty, rear also NULL
    free(temp);                // delete old front
}
```
👉 **Think:** People leave the line from the front.  

